{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"492423553055931673f361b6fb74533c2b6010547bab018285d416851d581bb9","digest":{"component_or_area":"DC adapter pagination structural test","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py","test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size","_TRANSPORT_SRC","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default()","commit 4213081d23"],"problem_keywords":["structural guard","vacuous predicate","module split","AST scan","pagination","search_issues"],"propositions":["The structural guard _search_issues_calls_taking_the_default() scans only transport.py, which no longer contains any search_issues calls after commit 465d's module split relocated pagination logic to _base.py and _issues.py","The guard's predicate now returns an empty list unconditionally, causing test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size to pass vacuously and fail to catch unpaginated search_issues calls added elsewhere in the DC adapter","The scan path was hardcoded and never updated when code was moved, violating the guard's own documented contract that it must prevent silent truncation past page boundaries","Widening the scan to all *.py modules in adapters/jira_datacenter/ with a non-vacuity assertion ensures future module relocations cannot silently disarm the guard"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787395336958800292,"uuid":"84e7e7d3-be19-4134-8ee4-a7fc997fdd42"}